course: dictionary
lesson: 12843
title: Meeting and facing: the word encounter
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To encounter means to meet someone or something, often by chance. «On the way home, we encountered a fox in the park.» Nobody planned that meeting; it just happened.
explain: Encounter can also mean to face a problem or difficulty. «The team encountered heavy rain halfway up the mountain.» Here the team did not meet a person. They had to deal with the rain. Ask yourself: what did they meet? If the answer is a problem, encounter means face it.
explain: As a noun, an encounter is a meeting, especially one that is unexpected, strange or dangerous. «Her chance encounter with an old friend made her smile.» Test your meaning by swapping in meet or come across. If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: To encounter means to meet or come across someone or something, often by chance.
fact: To encounter a problem means to face it, as in «We encountered heavy traffic.»
fact: An encounter is a meeting, especially one that is unexpected, strange or dangerous.
fact: «Encounter» is often used in formal writing and exams instead of «meet» or «come across».
fact: Useful phrases: encounter difficulties, a chance encounter, a close encounter, encounter with.
exercise: «In the forest we encountered a bear.» What does encountered mean here? | Drew a picture of it | Forgot all about it | *Met by chance | Ran away from it
exercise: «The climbers encountered strong winds near the top.» What did the climbers do with the winds? | Enjoyed them | Went home to sleep | Hid from them as a game | *Faced them
exercise: Which word means a surprising meeting? | Lesson | Journey | Garden | *Encounter
test: «Across the field, the hikers encountered a herd of cows.» What does encountered most nearly mean? | Watched from far away | Painted | *Came upon, unexpectedly | Counted
test: «The new road encountered problems: floods and delays.» Which meaning fits encountered here? | Cleaned them | *Faced them | Avoided them | Celebrated them
exam: Which sentence uses encounter to mean face a difficulty? | *The team encountered serious delays on the road | Mia encountered her cousin at the shop | The dog encountered its bowl at dinner | We encountered a film about bears
